{
  "_comment": [
    "Pinned inventory of the Picogrid Legion resource schemas the FORMAT_COVERAGE.md row",
    "set was written against. Legion is a VENDOR API: unlike a ratified standard it can",
    "change between deploys, and its info.version demonstrably does not move when it does.",
    "So the row set is only trustworthy against a named document, and this file is that",
    "document's field list plus its hash. tests/test_cdm_format_coverage.py walks it and",
    "fails the build on a field with no row -- which is how 'every field of every in-scope",
    "resource' becomes a checkable claim rather than a sentence.",
    "Regenerate ONLY by re-fetching the spec and re-reading the diff; a field appearing here",
    "without a row in the table is the gate working, not a nuisance."
  ],
